window.MONSTER_CHUNK_83 = [{"name":"Umdhlebi","cr":12,"xp":19200,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"plant","init":5,"senses":[{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":27,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":26,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +18 natural, -2 size","hp":178,"hd":"17d8+102","hdvalue":17,"fort":15,"ref":8,"will":8,"dr":"10/magic slashing or bludgeoning","immunities":["plant traits"],"weaknesses":["fire"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":10}],"melee":"2 slam +21 (3d8+10/19-20 plus grab)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"compelling whisper"},{"type":"constrict","details":"3d8+10"}],"strength":30,"dexterity":13,"constitution":20,"intelligence":9,"wisdom":12,"charisma":15,"baseatk":12,"cmb":24,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":35,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Improved Disarm"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Trip"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Lunge"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Toughness"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":0},{"skill":"Perception","value":12},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":6},{"skill":"Stealth","value":0},{"skill":"Survival","value":4}],"sq":[{"type":"treacherous ground"},{"type":"writhing tendrils"}],"environments":["tropical forests","tropical jungles"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"What appeared at first glance to be the decaying husk of an enormous tree erupts into motion, as thick tendrils reach outward hungrily from all sides. Amid the jumble of motion, a subconscious whisper promises sleep and sweet rest to any that lie down at the thing's base.","source":"AP 41","special_abilities":[{"type":"Compelling Whisper","kind":"Su","details":"As a standard action, an umdhlebi can entice any humanoid creature within 30 ft. to approach and lie down at the base of its trunk. This acts as a suggestion spell, but the umdhlebi can only compel this one action. A creature that makes a DC 20 Will save is unaffected, and is immune to the same umdhlebi's compelling whisper for 24 hours. An umdhlebi can also use this ability on creatures it is grappling, increasing the DC to 25. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Treacherous Ground","kind":"Ex","details":"The mass of gnashing roots and stems at the base of an umdhlebi's trunk are constantly in motion. As a result, all squares within 5 ft. of the umdhlebi's space are treated as difficult terrain for the purposes of movement through the area."},{"type":"Writhing Tendrils","kind":"Ex","details":"All umdhlebis have eight tendrils, but the creature can only make 2 slam attacks in a single round. However, an umdhlebi can continue to make 2 slam attacks even while its other tendrils are grappling or constricting. An umdhlebi can use this ability as long as it has two or more tendrils free to attack."}],"description":"Umdhlebis are massive, intelligent, and carnivorous plants that take root in jungles. Their outer shell is brown and resembles the thick bark of a dead tree, while concealing the softer layer of green cellulose beneath.\n\nWhen they flower, umdhlebis grow broad, fragile-looking crimson leaves with sharp, grasping edges. Umdhlebis draw their prey close with mind-affecting suggestions, enticing would-be victims to rest at the plant's base, and then strike with their vine-like tendrils, each as thick as a man's forearm.\n\nUmdhlebis grow to almost 20 ft. in height, but can be shorter or taller depending on the surrounding vegetation.\n\nAn umdhlebi's trunk ranges from 3 to 5 ft. in diameter, and the plant as a whole weighs over 10,000 pounds.\n\nUmdhlebis can live for up to 50 years.\n\nEcology Legends say that the first umdhlebi was created when an assassin vine crawled into the hollow corpse of a slain, jungle-dwelling treant. The creatures fused together, returning the treant to life, but instilling in it a devastating hunger. Regardless of its true origins, the umdhlebi is known and feared throughout the jungles of the world. Resembling a tree with a hard outer coating, the umdhlebi is actually an intelligent and mobile plant, capable of uprooting itself to find food or escape danger.\n\nAlthough ambulatory, the umdhlebi is too slow to truly hunt and has evolved several methods to attract prey. An umdhlebi uses its large vines and brightly colored leaves to draw in animals and other creatures of lesser intelligence.\n\nOnce in range, the umdhlebi lashes out with its strong, vine-like tendrils, enveloping and crushing its prey with bone-shattering force. Umdhlebis, however, prefer to feed on humanoids and can compel even the most strongminded individuals to approach their waiting snares.\n\nWhen sensing a nearby humanoid, an umdhlebi vibrates rows of fine, cilia-like hairs along its trunk, producing a sound that targets the minds of any close enough to hear it. This enticing drone causes those under its sway to approach the base of the tree where the umdhlebi can strike. Although the majority of an umdhlebi grows aboveground, the creature's mouth and digestive system are just below the surface. Large, thick roots at the base provide stability and allow for movement, but between these larger roots and beneath the umdhlebi's central trunk exists a populous network of long, thin stems.\n\nEach of these growths ends in double-sided fronds lined with spine-like teeth, similar to the leaves of a flytrap.\n\nWhen an umdhlebi roots itself to the ground, these stems burrow up to breach the surrounding earth, forming a moss-like border around the larger roots. Fresh kills are thus devoured from beneath, as the umdhlebi's understems feed. Numbering in the thousands, the umdhlebi's tiny mouths can strip a human carcass to its bones in under an hour, and although these under-stems are too small to effectively damage foes in melee, their shifting, undulating motion of makes traversing the ground around an umdhlebi difficult.\n\nUmdhlebis produce a spiny red fruit twice a year. This fruit appears similar to the seed pods of chestnut trees, but instead of holding tough seeds, it contains a bland meat riddled with dozens of triangular seeds. While wellfed umdhlebis sometimes allow monkeys and birds to pluck their fruit and carry it to new ground, they often use their own tendrils to pick and fling the fruit where they please. Some stories tell of undhlebis braining wanderers with these dense pods, or of passersby warned of the dangerous plants by their flying fruit, but these seasonal growths never reliably serve as weapons or warnings. Some tribes maintain dangerous traditions of seeking out and collecting undhlebi fruit to use in the creation of mashes or alcohols. Such products possess a distinctive dry-bitter taste and so are only prepared for use in coming-of-age rituals or other rites of passage.\n\nHabitat & Society Umdhlebis root themselves along roads and waterways near humanoid settlements whenever possible. As their roots are highly sensitive to vibrations and can detect the movement of other nearby creatures, they can stay out of sight, despite their size, and still be aware of their surroundings.\n\nAs the dry shell of their outer layer is particularly susceptible to fire, umdhlebis always entwine themselves with surrounding foliage so that any such attacks against them also risk setting the entire wilderness ablaze. If threatened and such cover isn't available, umdhlebis use their compelling whisper ability to manipulate one or more opponents and then draw them in to surround the plant's trunk, using them as living shields. Although they have no use for treasure, umdhlebis pile any leftover items from their prey into the base of their trunks as bait for passersby.\n\nWhen an umdhlebi moves on to other hunting grounds, it sheds its fruit first, hoping that the seeds will take hold and grow.\n\nDenizens of the Mwangi Expanse and other jungles are taught to recognize and burn umdhlebi seeds from an early age.\n\nNevertheless, some umdhlebi seeds do make their way into the earth and take root, reaching maturity with frightening speed.","ecology":"Legends say that the first umdhlebi was created when an assassin vine crawled into the hollow corpse of a slain, jungle-dwelling treant. The creatures fused together, returning the treant to life, but instilling in it a devastating hunger. Regardless of its true origins, the umdhlebi is known and feared throughout the jungles of the world. Resembling a tree with a hard outer coating, the umdhlebi is actually an intelligent and mobile plant, capable of uprooting itself to find food or escape danger.\n\nAlthough ambulatory, the umdhlebi is too slow to truly hunt and has evolved several methods to attract prey. An umdhlebi uses its large vines and brightly colored leaves to draw in animals and other creatures of lesser intelligence.\n\nOnce in range, the umdhlebi lashes out with its strong, vine-like tendrils, enveloping and crushing its prey with bone-shattering force. Umdhlebis, however, prefer to feed on humanoids and can compel even the most strongminded individuals to approach their waiting snares.\n\nWhen sensing a nearby humanoid, an umdhlebi vibrates rows of fine, cilia-like hairs along its trunk, producing a sound that targets the minds of any close enough to hear it. This enticing drone causes those under its sway to approach the base of the tree where the umdhlebi can strike. Although the majority of an umdhlebi grows aboveground, the creature's mouth and digestive system are just below the surface. Large, thick roots at the base provide stability and allow for movement, but between these larger roots and beneath the umdhlebi's central trunk exists a populous network of long, thin stems.\n\nEach of these growths ends in double-sided fronds lined with spine-like teeth, similar to the leaves of a flytrap.\n\nWhen an umdhlebi roots itself to the ground, these stems burrow up to breach the surrounding earth, forming a moss-like border around the larger roots. Fresh kills are thus devoured from beneath, as the umdhlebi's understems feed. Numbering in the thousands, the umdhlebi's tiny mouths can strip a human carcass to its bones in under an hour, and although these under-stems are too small to effectively damage foes in melee, their shifting, undulating motion of makes traversing the ground around an umdhlebi difficult.\n\nUmdhlebis produce a spiny red fruit twice a year. This fruit appears similar to the seed pods of chestnut trees, but instead of holding tough seeds, it contains a bland meat riddled with dozens of triangular seeds. While wellfed umdhlebis sometimes allow monkeys and birds to pluck their fruit and carry it to new ground, they often use their own tendrils to pick and fling the fruit where they please. Some stories tell of undhlebis braining wanderers with these dense pods, or of passersby warned of the dangerous plants by their flying fruit, but these seasonal growths never reliably serve as weapons or warnings. Some tribes maintain dangerous traditions of seeking out and collecting undhlebi fruit to use in the creation of mashes or alcohols. Such products possess a distinctive dry-bitter taste and so are only prepared for use in coming-of-age rituals or other rites of passage.","habitat_society":"Umdhlebis root themselves along roads and waterways near humanoid settlements whenever possible. As their roots are highly sensitive to vibrations and can detect the movement of other nearby creatures, they can stay out of sight, despite their size, and still be aware of their surroundings.\n\nAs the dry shell of their outer layer is particularly susceptible to fire, umdhlebis always entwine themselves with surrounding foliage so that any such attacks against them also risk setting the entire wilderness ablaze. If threatened and such cover isn't available, umdhlebis use their compelling whisper ability to manipulate one or more opponents and then draw them in to surround the plant's trunk, using them as living shields. Although they have no use for treasure, umdhlebis pile any leftover items from their prey into the base of their trunks as bait for passersby.\n\nWhen an umdhlebi moves on to other hunting grounds, it sheds its fruit first, hoping that the seeds will take hold and grow.\n\nDenizens of the Mwangi Expanse and other jungles are taught to recognize and burn umdhlebi seeds from an early age.\n\nNevertheless, some umdhlebi seeds do make their way into the earth and take root, reaching maturity with frightening speed."},{"name":"Valkyrie","cr":12,"xp":19200,"alignment":"CN","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["extraplanar"],"init":3,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"deathwatch"}],"ac":27,"ac_touch":19,"ac_flat_footed":24,"ac_mods":"+8 armor, +6 deflection, +3 Dex, +0 natural","hp":168,"hd":"16d10+80","hdvalue":16,"fort":10,"ref":13,"will":15,"dr":"10/cold iron and lawful","immunities":["cold","electricity","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":23,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"fly","speed":100,"maneuverability":"perfect"}],"melee":"+2 returning spear +23 (1d8+8/x3)","ranged":"+2 returning spear +22 (1d8+6/x3)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","spell_like_abilities_caster_level":12,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":17,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"deathwatch"},{"spell":"tongues"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"aid"},{"spell":"death ward"},{"spell":"gentle repose"},{"spell":"plane shift","details":"self and mount only"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"breath of life"},{"spell":"heal"},{"spell":"summon","details":"level 8, 1 sleipnir 100%"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"call lightning storm"},{"spell":"divine power"},{"spell":"geas/quest"}]}],"strength":18,"dexterity":17,"constitution":20,"intelligence":13,"wisdom":20,"charisma":23,"baseatk":16,"cmb":20,"cmd":39,"feats":[{"feat":"Mounted Combat"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Ride-By Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Ride)"},{"feat":"Spirited Charge"},{"feat":"Trample"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (spear)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":27},{"skill":"Handle Animal","value":25},{"skill":"Heal","value":24},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":20},{"skill":"Perception","value":24},{"skill":"Ride","value":28},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":24}],"languages":["Celestial","Common","tongues"],"sq":[{"type":"battle trained"},{"type":"choose the slain"},{"type":"holy zeal"}],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","ride (2-8 valkyries)"],"treasure":"triple (+2 breastplate, +2 returning spear)","description_visual":"Surrounded by lightning, this impressive female warrior wears a gleaming golden breastplate and carries a shining spear.","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 3","special_abilities":[{"type":"Battle Trained","kind":"Ex","details":"A valkyrie is proficient with all armor. Armor never impacts a valkyrie's speed, nor does a valkyrie take armor check penalties on Ride checks."},{"type":"Choose the Slain","kind":"Su","details":"A valkyrie can draw the soul from a newly dead body and store it in her spear for transport to the Outer Planes. This functions as soul bind, but the dead creature must be willing to have its soul taken. If the creature is unwilling, this ability has no effect."},{"type":"Holy Zeal","kind":"Su","details":"A valkyrie adds her Charisma modifier as a deflection bonus to her Armor Class."}],"description":"Valkyries are outsiders who scour the battlefields of the Material Plane for warriors of great prowess and legendary renown. With a glance, a valkyrie can tell who is near death and ready to give up life and who fights on to live another day, and can either claim the soul of the slain or aid the living to continue the fight.\n\nValkyries are always female, and appear as strong and beautiful human, dwarven, or elven women. A human valkyrie is 6 ft. tall and weighs close to 200 pounds.\n\nValkyries serve a variety of deities, though they are most often associated with the gods of war, conf lict, valor, and courage. Although capable combatants in their own right, valkyries are almost always encountered mounted, typically on flying steeds such as dragon horses, pegasi, or sleipnirs.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Vespergaunt","cr":12,"xp":19200,"alignment":"NE","size":"Medium","type":"ooze","init":6,"senses":[{"type":"all-around vision"},{"type":"blindsight","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"true seeing"}],"auras":["madness (60 ft., DC 21)"],"ac":20,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":18,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +8 natural","hp":195,"hd":"17d8+119","hdvalue":17,"fort":14,"ref":9,"will":9,"defensive_abilities":["amorphous"],"dr":"10/aligned","immunities":["ooze traits"],"sr":23,"weaknesses":["light sensitivity"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":10},{"type":"fly","speed":60,"maneuverability":"perfect"}],"melee":"2 slams +21 (2d8+8 plus siphon spirit)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","spell_like_abilities_caster_level":17,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":24,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"tongues"},{"spell":"true seeing"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"deeper darkness"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"contact other plane"}]},{"frequency":"1/month","spells":[{"spell":"wish"}]}],"strength":27,"dexterity":14,"constitution":24,"intelligence":15,"wisdom":15,"charisma":16,"baseatk":12,"cmb":20,"cmd":32,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Persuasive"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (slam)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":10},{"skill":"Fly","value":15},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":17},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":19},{"skill":"Perception","value":22},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":12},{"skill":"Stealth","value":12}],"languages":["tongues","telepathy 100 ft."],"sq":[{"type":"no breath"}],"environments":["any (Aucturn)"],"organizations":["solitary","convocation (2-4)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This amorphous mass of eyes, tentacles, and green vapor vaguely resembles a jumble of rotten brain matter.","source":"Inner Sea Bestiary","special_abilities":[{"type":"Aura of Madness","kind":"Su","details":"Any creature within a 60-foot radius of the vespergaunt must succeed at a DC 21 save or be confused for 1d4 rounds. Once a creature successfully saves, it cannot be affected by the same vespergaunt's aura again for 24 hours. As a free action, the vespergaunt can suppress its aura. This is a mind-affecting effect. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Damage Reduction","kind":"Su","details":"A vespergaunt's damage reduction is bypassed by any weapons that are chaos-, evil-, good-, or law-aligned."},{"type":"Siphon Spirit","kind":"Su","details":"Any creature touched by a vespergaunt must succeed at a DC 21 Will save or gain 1 negative level as the vespergaunt rips away a portion of its soul. A divine spellcaster gains an additional negative level with each failed save. The victim must save anew each time it is touched, and a character killed by this attack disintegrates completely except for its eyes and strands of brain matter, which become part of the vespergaunt. Only powerful magic such as miracle or wish can resurrect a creature slain in this manner."}],"description":"Often called \"heresy oozes,\" vespergaunts are emissaries and tools of the horrible god-things of the Dark Tapestry. Found primarily on Aucturn, vespergaunts act as spiritual conduits for those attempting to contact the Great Old Ones, collecting and relaying those prayers deemed worthy while also preparing inhabited worlds for the coming of the Dominion of the Black. A typical vespergaunt is 8 ft. tall and 6 ft. wide, and weighs just 50 pounds.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Voidstick Zombie","cr":12,"xp":19200,"alignment":"CE","size":"Medium","type":"undead","init":4,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"lifesense","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["sacrilegious aura"],"ac":26,"ac_touch":14,"ac_flat_footed":26,"ac_mods":"+12 natural, +4 profane","hp":157,"hd":"15d8+90","hdvalue":15,"hp_mods":["fast healing 3"],"fort":9,"ref":7,"will":9,"defensive_abilities":["channel resistance +4"],"immunities":["undead traits"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"2 melee touch +13 (1d8 negative energy)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"channel negative energy","details":"5/day, DC 22, 8d6"}],"strength":12,"dexterity":11,"intelligence":7,"wisdom":6,"charisma":15,"baseatk":11,"cmb":12,"cmd":26,"feats":[{"feat":"Channel Smite"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Channel"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Stealth)"},{"feat":"Toughness"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":5},{"skill":"Perception","value":10},{"skill":"Stealth","value":11}],"languages":["Common"],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","plague (3-9)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This shambling humanoid's taut gray skin shows signs of arcane symbols now faded with age and decay. Long, darkwood spikes riddle its body; every inch of flesh is staked and violated. A palpable aura of entropy and despair hangs over the sorry, perforated creature.","source":"AP 57","special_abilities":[{"type":"Channel Energy","kind":"Su","details":"The voidstick zombie can channel negative energy as a 15th-level cleric."},{"type":"Sacrilegious Aura","kind":"Sp","details":"The overwhelming entropic energies and the sheer number of voidsticks animating the voidstick zombie warp and augment negative and positive energy around the creature. As with all voidsticks, an aura of intense negative energy extends in a 30-foot radius from the zombie functioning as the spell desecrate. Undead within this aura receive a +1 profane bonus on attack and damage rolls and the DC to resist channeled negative energy increases by +3. The voidstick zombie constantly gains the benefits of this effect (the attack and damage bonuses are already incorporated into its statistics). In addition, this miasma of void energies also interferes with wielding positive energy. Any creature attempting to use positive energy in this area-such as through a cleric's channel energy ability, a paladin's lay on hands, or any spell with the healing descriptor-must make a DC 25 concentration check. If this check fails, the effect is blocked, consuming one use of the ability, or the spell is lost."}],"description":"The voidstick zombie is the hateful creation of wicked shamans and necromancers, who use voidsticks to animate the dead. One voidstick is required for every Hit Die possessed by the base creature. These vile devices, each of which is 6 to 10 inches in length, are pierced through the living or dead body of a creature, pumping the dark energy of the void into its form. Packed with the bitter entropy of negative energy, the creature rises, seeking out the life force of others with endless sadness and insane determination. Its single goal is to extinguish life and smother any source of positive energy. Multiple voidsticks in a creature's form feed one another, augmenting their standard abilities and imbuing the touch of the voidstick zombie with the power to drain life from anything it touches. The zombie becomes almost a sliver of the void itself, existing in a state of such negative power that its very proximity can tamper with other creatures' abilities to summon the powers of the Positive Energy Plane, and with the perpetual sadness that numbs its own intellect it gains the power to enhance and inf luence other creatures that depend on negative energy.\n\nThese sad creatures, wracked with soulless negative energy, constantly hunger for destruction, delighted at every chance they get to snuff the spark of life from the living. They hunt the islands throughout the Shackles, especially the Cannibal Isles, where their creation began long before its current inhabitants made their home there.\n\nAs the brutal and savage kuru people of the Cannibal Isles explored the ruins of Ghol-Gan, they discovered the foul magic involved with the voidsticks, and as they turned to barbarism and cannibalism, their shamans carved these devices and created the first voidstick zombie seen on Golarion in thousands of years. The kuru use voidstick zombies for war against each other and to serve as ruthless hunters, culling humanoids who wander too close to their blood-drenched islands. Kuru shamans create the vile voidsticks in order to enhance their own necromantic strength as well as to animate voidstick zombies. In some tribes it is seen as a great honor to be transformed into one of these powerful creatures, and some aged shamans on the eve of their death elect to undergo this transformation instead of becoming a ritual meal for their tribes.\n\nSince the rediscovery of voidsticks, those interested in necromancy and the creation of new undead have sent emissaries to the Shackles eager to buy them. These enterprising necromancers experiment with the devices and unleash voidstick zombies into Avistan and Garund to fulfill their murderous intent.\n\nVoidsticks In remote parts of the world, it isn't always practical for the faithful to visit holy places with any regularity. In particular, the weak, the sick, and the dying may be in no position to trek across plains or risk dangerous water crossings to see their spiritual leaders. In response to this, the godstick was born-a crafted rod that serves as a portable shrine, carried by shamans and witchdoctors and pushed into the ground to focus devotion at any location. Ingenuity isn't just the way of the benign, however, and just as often it is the way of evil. Before long, shamans who worshiped more hateful deities corrupted this notion; they created the voidsticks and drove them into bodies, living or dead, charging those bodies with the power of the endless void and creating rattling, hungry abominations.\n\nVoidstick\n\nAura faint necromancy [evil]; CL 5\n\nSlot special; Price 2,500 gp, Weighs 1 lb.\n\nDESCRIPTION\n\nEach voidstick is 6 t0 10 inches long, with a diameter of about an inch. Carved from single pieces of polished darkwood, they often display markings or symbols sacred to the deity of their creator, but can just as easily be plain and smooth. Planting a voidstick into the ground with an appropriate prayer is a full-round action that provokes attacks of opportunity. The device floods the area with negative energy, producing an effect identical to the desecrate spell in a 20- foot radius. In addition, any evil divine caster within 20 ft. of the voidstick may cast her spells without the need for any material component with a value of 10 gp or less, or any focus item with a value of 50 gp or less. This ability functions only for the individual planting the voidstick and persists until the stick is uprooted.\n\nWhile this is a useful tool for shamans in locations poorly serviced by trade in magical goods, it pales in comparison to the voidstick's most potent function: the creation of undead. Creating a voidstick zombie requires an hour-long ritual during which foul symbols are drawn across a corpse's flesh. At the end of the hour, the creator must make a DC 25 Knowledge (religion) check before driving the first voidstick into the victim's heart. If this check succeeds, the victim is transformed into a voidstick zombie. To fully animate the creature, one voidstick must be used for each Hit Die the base creature has. In 12 rounds, the creature rises under its own power, eager to spread its negative energy and snuff out life nearby. Undead created using voidsticks are not under the control of their creator but can be commanded using channeled negative energy, spells, or similar effects.\n\nVoidsticks can also be driven into a living body to slay the creature and transition it to undeath. If a living body is used, the creature must be pinned or otherwise helpless for the duration of the entire ritual. When the ritual is complete and the first voidstick is inserted, the creature must make a DC 18 Fortitude save. If this save succeeds, the creature is reduced to 0 hit points and is dying, but the magic of the voidstick and the ritual are wasted and the ritual must be performed again, using another voidstick. If the save fails, the creature dies and the ritual is successful, transforming the base creature into a voidstick zombie.\n\nUndead that contain such an item benefit from the +2 bonus hit points per Hit Die for having been created in the area of an enhanced desecrate spell.\n\nCONSTRUCTION\n\nRequirements Craft Wondrous Item, animate dead, desecrate; Creator must have 5 ranks in Knowledge (religion). Cost 1,750 gp","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Vouivre","cr":12,"xp":19200,"alignment":"CE","size":"Large","type":"monstrous humanoid","subtypes":["aquatic"],"init":5,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":27,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":26,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +17 natural, -1 size","hp":152,"hd":"16d10+64","hdvalue":16,"fort":9,"ref":11,"will":14,"save_mods":"+4 vs. mind-affecting effects","defensive_abilities":["unwavering mind"],"immunities":["cold"],"resists":[{"type":"fire","value":10},{"type":"sonic","value":10}],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"fly","speed":40,"maneuverability":"poor"},{"type":"swim","speed":50}],"melee":"bite +20 (3d6+4 plus grab), 2 claws +20 (2d6+4/19-20), 2 wings +14 (1d8+2)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"30-ft. cone, 8d6 fire, Reflex DC 22 half, usable every 1d4 rounds"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":13,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":17,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"charm person"},{"spell":"comprehend languages"},{"spell":"ghost sound"},{"spell":"speak with animals","details":"snakes only"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"charm animal","details":"snakes only"},{"spell":"shout"},{"spell":"song of discord"}]}],"strength":19,"dexterity":13,"constitution":18,"intelligence":11,"wisdom":14,"charisma":18,"baseatk":16,"cmb":21,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":32,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Critical Focus"},{"feat":"Deafening Critical"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (claw)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (claw)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":20},{"skill":"Fly","value":6},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":15},{"skill":"Perception","value":17},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":10},{"skill":"Stealth","value":12},{"skill":"Swim","value":12}],"languages":["Common","Sylvan"],"sq":[{"type":"amphibious"},{"type":"snake empathy"}],"environments":["any lakes","any rivers","temperate forests"],"organizations":["solitary","harem (1 plus 4-10 snakes)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"One half of this creature is a nude woman, and the other is the front end of a slithering, winged dragon.","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 4","special_abilities":[{"type":"Snake Empathy","kind":"Ex","details":"A vouivre can communicate and empathize with snakes. It can use Diplomacy to alter such an animal's attitude, and when doing so gains a +4 racial bonus on the check."},{"type":"Unwavering Mind","kind":"Ex","details":"A vouivre gains a +4 bonus on saving throws to resist mind-affecting effects."}],"description":"A vouivre is a deceptive and monstrous predator that looks like a humanoid woman from the waist up and the front end of a green-scaled dragon from the waist down. It shuns the company of its own kind, preferring evil fey (particularly water-dwelling ones such as nixies) for intelligent conversation and mundane snakes for companionship. A vouivre is 12 ft. long from head to head, weighs 500 pounds, and can live 200 years. Vouivres make their homes in small caves near calm waters. They like to decorate their lairs with shiny coins, jewelry, and bright silks. One might place some of its treasure in the water outside to lure in curious humanoids, and bathe in these waters as a further enticement, hiding its reptilian half until prey is within striking distance. Because a vouivre can breathe water or air (from either head), it often grabs a creature, then retreats underwater to wait for the opponent to drown. It prefers humanoid flesh, but will feed on any available warm-blooded prey. Vouivres have an affinity for music, and their magic is often accompanied by singing or subtle musical vibrations from their scales. When a vouivre dies, its dragon head disgorges a 2-foot-diameter glassy egg. After around 6 weeks, the egg hatches into one or two vouivres, which take 7 years to reach maturity. These offspring resemble humanoids the mother has eaten, so it prefers to feast on attractive and strong victims. The young also adapt to the appearance of nearby reptilian creatures.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Young Adult Blue Dragon","cr":12,"xp":19200,"alignment":"LE","size":"Huge","type":"dragon","subtypes":["earth"],"init":4,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"}],"auras":["frightful presence (150 ft., DC 19)"],"ac":25,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":25,"ac_mods":"+17 natural, -2 size","hp":147,"hd":"14d12+56","hdvalue":14,"fort":13,"ref":9,"will":11,"dr":"5/magic","immunities":["electricity","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":23,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"burrow","speed":20},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"bite +20 (2d8+10), 2 claws +19 (2d6+7), 2 wings +17 (1d8+3), tail slap +17 (2d6+10)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"100-ft. line, DC 21, 10d8 electricity"},{"type":"crush","details":"Small creatures, DC 21, 2d8+10"},{"type":"desert thirst","details":"DC 21"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":14,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":22,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"ghost sound"},{"spell":"minor image"}]}],"spellsknown_caster_level":3,"spellsknown_concentration":11,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":6,"spells":[{"spell":"mage armor"},{"spell":"shield"},{"spell":"true strike"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"arcane mark"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"mage hand"},{"spell":"read magic"},{"spell":"resistance"}]}],"strength":25,"dexterity":10,"constitution":19,"intelligence":14,"wisdom":15,"charisma":14,"baseatk":14,"cmb":23,"cmd":33,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Combat Casting"},{"feat":"Dazzling Display"},{"feat":"Hover"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Shatter Defenses"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":19},{"skill":"Fly","value":9},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":19},{"skill":"Knowledge (local)","value":19},{"skill":"Perception","value":19},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":19},{"skill":"Stealth","value":9},{"skill":"Survival","value":19}],"languages":["Auran","Common","Draconic"],"sq":[{"type":"sound imitation"}],"environments":["warm deserts"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"With scales the color of the desert sky, this large, serpentine dragon moves with an unsettling grace.","group":"Chromatic Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary","special_abilities":[{"type":"Desert Thirst","kind":"Su","details":"A blue dragon can cast create water at will (CL 14). Alternatively, it can destroy an equal amount of liquid in a 10-foot burst. Unattended liquids are instantly reduced to sand. Liquid-based magic items (such as potions) and items in a creature's possession must succeed on a Will save (DC 21) or be destroyed."},{"type":"Sound Imitation","kind":"Ex","details":"A very young or older blue dragon can mimic any voice or sound it has heard by making a successful Bluff check against a listener's Sense Motive check."}],"description":"Blue dragons are consummate schemers and obsessively orderly. In combat, blue dragons prefer to surprise foes if possible, and are not above retreating if the odds turn against them. They prefer to lair near those that they control, sometimes even within the confines of a city.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Young Adult Bronze Dragon","cr":12,"xp":19200,"alignment":"LG","size":"Huge","type":"dragon","subtypes":["water"],"init":0,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"}],"ac":25,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":25,"ac_mods":"+17 natural, -2 size","hp":147,"hd":"14d12+56","hdvalue":14,"fort":13,"ref":9,"will":13,"dr":"5/magic","immunities":["electricity","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":23,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"},{"type":"swim","speed":60}],"melee":"bite +19 (2d8+10), 2 claws +19 (2d6+7), tail slap +17 (2d6+10), 2 wings +17 (1d8+3)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"100-ft. line, DC 21, 10d6 electricity"},{"type":"crush","details":"2d8+10, DC 21"},{"type":"repulsion breath"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":14,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":18,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"create food and water"},{"spell":"speak with animals"}]}],"spellsknown_caster":"sorcerer","spellsknown_caster_level":5,"spellsknown_concentration":9,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"blur"},{"spell":"mirror image"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"alarm"},{"spell":"mage armor"},{"spell":"obscuring mist"},{"spell":"true strike"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"light"},{"spell":"mage hand"},{"spell":"message"},{"spell":"resistance"},{"spell":"prestidigitation"}]}],"strength":25,"dexterity":10,"constitution":19,"intelligence":18,"wisdom":19,"charisma":18,"baseatk":14,"cmb":23,"cmd":33,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Improved Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":21},{"skill":"Fly","value":9},{"skill":"Handle Animal","value":18},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":21},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":21},{"skill":"Perception","value":25},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":25},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":21},{"skill":"Stealth","value":9},{"skill":"Swim","value":32}],"languages":["Aquan","Common","Draconic","Elven","Gnome"],"sq":[{"type":"change shape","details":"animal or humanoid, polymorph"},{"type":"water breathing"},{"type":"wave mastery","details":"50 min"}],"environments":["temperate coastlines"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"This sleek dragon is covered in dull metallic scales that range in color from shining bronze to mottled blue.","group":"Metallic Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary","special_abilities":[{"type":"Repulsion Breath","kind":"Su","details":"Instead of a line of electricity, a bronze dragon can breathe a cone of repulsion gas. Targets must make a Will save or be compelled to do nothing but move away from the dragon for 1d6 rounds plus 1 round per age category. This is a mind-affecting compulsion effect."},{"type":"Water Breathing","kind":"Ex","details":"A bronze dragon breathes water and can use its breath weapon, spells, and abilities underwater."},{"type":"Wave Mastery","kind":"Su","details":"For up to 10 minutes per age category per day, a juvenile bronze dragon, along with creatures or vessels within 50 ft., can move at twice its normal speed in water."}],"description":"Bronze dragons have been known to ally with travelers and adventurers if the cause and reward is right and just.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Abrakarn Viper","cr":13,"xp":25600,"alignment":"CE","size":"Huge","type":"construct","subtypes":["chaotic","evil"],"init":3,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"120 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":30,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":27,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +19 natural, -2 size","hp":139,"hd":"18d10+40","hdvalue":18,"fort":6,"ref":9,"will":10,"dr":"10/-","immunities":["construct traits"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"electricity","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":24,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40}],"melee":"3 bites +25 (2d8+9 plus poison)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"confusing critical"},{"type":"poison"}],"strength":28,"dexterity":17,"wisdom":19,"charisma":1,"baseatk":18,"cmb":29,"cmd":42,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","sq":[{"type":"demon-souled"},{"type":"find master"},{"type":"guard"},{"type":"shield other"}],"environments":["any land"],"organizations":["solitary","pair"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This massive, three-headed clockwork snake is crafted of brass and strange, dark alloys.","source":"Monster Codex","special_abilities":[{"type":"Confusing Critical","kind":"Sp","details":"If an abrakarn viper confirms a critical hit against an opponent with its bite attack, the opponent must succeed at a DC 23 Will save or be confused for 1 round (as lesser confusion). The save DC is Charisma-based and includes a +9 racial bonus."},{"type":"Demon-Souled","kind":"Ex","details":"Bound demonic life force animates the viper, giving it the chaotic and evil subtypes."},{"type":"Find Master","kind":"Su","details":"As long as an abrakarn viper and its diadem are on the same plane, the viper can unerringly find the diadem's wearer (or just the diadem, if it is removed)."},{"type":"Guard","kind":"Ex","details":"If so ordered, an abrakarn viper defends the wearer of the diadem. All attacks against the diadem's wearer take a -2 penalty when the wearer is within the viper's melee reach."},{"type":"Poison","kind":"Ex","details":"An abrakarn viper's bite injects poison from a hidden reservoir within its body. The creator must refill this reservoir manually. The reservoir holds enough poison for three successful bite attacks, after which the creature merely deals bite damage. Refilling the reservoir takes 5 rounds and provokes attacks of opportunity. The creator can fill the reservoir with any injury poison (typically drow poison)."},{"type":"Shield Other","kind":"Sp","details":"The wearer of an abrakarn viper's diadem can activate this ability as a standard action when within 100 ft. of the viper. This ability transfers half the damage that would be dealt to the diadem's wearer to the viper (this ability doesn't provide the bonuses to AC or on saving throws granted by the spell of the same name). Damage transferred in this way bypasses any defensive abilities the viper possesses (such as immunity or damage reduction)."}],"description":"Demonic spirits imbue this serpentine construct with the unnatural power to protect anyone who wears its diadem of control.\n\nConstruction\n\nAn abrakarn viper's body and its diadem of control are built from 5,000 pounds of magically treated brass and rare metals costing 10,000 gp in total.\n\nABRAKARN VIPER\n\nCL 8th; Price 150,000 gp\n\nConstruction\n\nRequirements Craft Construct, animate object, confusion, geas/ quest, shield other; Skill Craft (armor), Craft (blacksmithing), or Craft (weapons) DC 21; Cost 80,000 gp","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Adult Blue Dragon","cr":13,"xp":25600,"alignment":"LE","size":"Huge","type":"dragon","subtypes":["earth"],"init":4,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"}],"auras":["electricity (5 ft., 1d6 elect.)","frightful presence (180 ft., DC 21)"],"ac":28,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":28,"ac_mods":"+20 natural, -2 size","hp":184,"hd":"16d12+80","hdvalue":16,"fort":15,"ref":10,"will":13,"dr":"5/magic","immunities":["electricity","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":24,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"burrow","speed":20},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"bite +23 (2d8+12), 2 claws +22 (2d6+8), 2 wings +20 (1d8+4), tail slap +20 (2d6+12)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"100-ft. line, DC 23, 12d8 electricity"},{"type":"crush"},{"type":"desert thirst","details":"DC 21"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":16,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":25,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"ghost sound"},{"spell":"minor image"},{"spell":"ventriloquism"}]}],"spellsknown_caster_level":5,"spellsknown_concentration":14,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"invisibility"},{"spell":"resist energy"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"alarm"},{"spell":"mage armor"},{"spell":"shield"},{"spell":"true strike"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"arcane mark"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"mage hand"},{"spell":"mending"},{"spell":"read magic"},{"spell":"resistance"}]}],"strength":27,"dexterity":10,"constitution":21,"intelligence":16,"wisdom":17,"charisma":16,"baseatk":16,"cmb":26,"cmd":36,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Combat Casting"},{"feat":"Dazzling Display"},{"feat":"Deadly Stroke"},{"feat":"Hover"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Shatter Defenses"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Appraise","value":22},{"skill":"Fly","value":11},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":22},{"skill":"Knowledge (local)","value":22},{"skill":"Knowledge (geography)","value":22},{"skill":"Perception","value":22},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":22},{"skill":"Stealth","value":11},{"skill":"Survival","value":22}],"languages":["Auran","Common","Draconic","Giant"],"sq":[{"type":"sound imitation"}],"environments":["warm deserts"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"With scales the color of the desert sky, this large, serpentine dragon moves with an unsettling grace.","group":"Chromatic Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary","special_abilities":[{"type":"Desert Thirst","kind":"Su","details":"A blue dragon can cast create water at will (CL equals its HD). Alternatively, it can destroy an equal amount of liquid in a 10-foot burst. Unattended liquids are instantly reduced to sand. Liquid-based magic items (such as potions) and items in a creature's possession must succeed on a Will save (DC equal to the dragon's breath weapon) or be destroyed. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Electricity Aura","kind":"Su","details":"An adult blue dragon is surrounded by an aura of electricity. Creatures within 5 ft. take 1d6 points of electricity damage at the beginning of the dragon's turn. An old dragon's aura extends to 10 ft. An ancient dragon's damage increases to 2d6."},{"type":"Mirage","kind":"Su","details":"An old or older blue dragon can make itself appear to be in two places at once as a free action for a number of rounds per day equal to its Hit Dice. This ability functions as project image but the dragon can use its breath weapon through the mirage."},{"type":"Sandstorm","kind":"Su","details":"As a standard action, a great wyrm blue dragon can create a sandstorm centered on itself with a radius of 1,200 ft. Creatures other than the dragon inside the storm take 2d6 points of damage per round in addition to the normal sandstorm penalties. This sandstorm lasts for up to 1 hour, but can be dismissed by the dragon as a free action."},{"type":"Sound Imitation","kind":"Ex","details":"A very young or older blue dragon can mimic any voice or sound it has heard by making a successful Bluff check against a listener's Sense Motive check."},{"type":"Spell-Like Abilities","kind":"Sp","details":"A blue dragon gains the following spell-like abilities, usable at will upon reaching the listed age category. Young-ghost sound; Juvenile-minor image; Adult-ventriloquism; Old-hallucinatory terrain; Ancient- veil; Great wyrm-mirage arcana."},{"type":"Storm Breath","kind":"Su","details":"An ancient or older blue dragon can use its breath weapon to create a storm of lightning. This functions as call lightning storm, but the damage is equal to the dragon's breath weapon. The dragon can call down 1 bolt per round as a free action for 1d6 rounds. The save DC is equal to the dragon's breath weapon DC. Additional uses of this ability extend the duration by an additional 1d6 rounds. Age Category S pecial Abilities Caster Level Wyrmling Desert thirst, immune to electricity - Very young Sound imitation - Young Ghost sound - Juvenile Frightful presence, minor image 1st Young adult DR 5/magic, spell resistance 3rd Adult Electricity aura, ventriloquism 5th Mature adult DR 10/magic 7th Old Mirage, hallucinatory terrain 9th Very old DR 15/magic 11th Ancient Storm breath, veil 13th Wyrm DR 20/magic 15th Great wyrm Sandstorm, mirage arcana 17th."}],"description":"Blue dragons are consummate schemers and obsessively orderly. In combat, blue dragons prefer to surprise foes if possible, and are not above retreating if the odds turn against them. They prefer to lair near those that they control, sometimes even within the confines of a city.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Adult Bronze Dragon","cr":13,"xp":25600,"alignment":"LG","size":"Huge","type":"dragon","subtypes":["water"],"init":0,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"}],"auras":["frightful presence (180 ft., DC 23)"],"ac":28,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":28,"ac_mods":"+20 natural, -2 size","hp":184,"hd":"16d12+80","hdvalue":16,"fort":15,"ref":10,"will":15,"dr":"5/magic","immunities":["electricity","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":24,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"},{"type":"swim","speed":60}],"melee":"bite +22 (2d8+12), 2 claws +22 (2d6+8), 2 wings +20 (1d8+4), tail slap +20 (2d6+12)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"100-ft. line, DC 23, 12d6 electricity"},{"type":"crush"},{"type":"repulsion breath"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":16,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":21,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"create food and water"},{"spell":"fog cloud"},{"spell":"speak with animals"}]}],"spellsknown_caster_level":7,"spellsknown_concentration":12,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"dispel magic"},{"spell":"slow"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"blur"},{"spell":"gust of wind"},{"spell":"mirror image"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":8,"spells":[{"spell":"alarm"},{"spell":"mage armor"},{"spell":"obscuring mist"},{"spell":"shield"},{"spell":"true strike"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"light"},{"spell":"message"},{"spell":"resistance"},{"spell":"2 more"}]}],"strength":27,"dexterity":10,"constitution":21,"intelligence":20,"wisdom":21,"charisma":20,"baseatk":16,"cmb":26,"cmd":36,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Hover"},{"feat":"Improved Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":24},{"skill":"Fly","value":11},{"skill":"Handle Animals","value":21},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":24},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":24},{"skill":"Knowledge (geography)","value":24},{"skill":"Perception","value":28},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":28},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":24},{"skill":"Stealth","value":11},{"skill":"Swim","value":35}],"languages":["Aquan","Common","Draconic","Elven","Gnome","2 more"],"sq":[{"type":"change shape"},{"type":"water breathing"},{"type":"wave mastery"}],"environments":["temperate coastlines"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"This sleek dragon is covered in dull metallic scales that range in color from shining bronze to mottled blue.","group":"Metallic Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary","special_abilities":[{"type":"Change Shape","kind":"Su","details":"A young or older bronze dragon can take any animal or humanoid form 3/day as if using polymorph."},{"type":"Electricity Aura","kind":"Su","details":"An old or older bronze dragon has an aura of electricity. All creatures within 5 ft. take 1d6 points of electricity damage at the start of the dragon's turn. An ancient dragon's aura is 10 ft. A great wyrm's damage increases to 2d6. A bronze dragon can suppress this aura at will."},{"type":"Repulsion Breath","kind":"Su","details":"Instead of a line of electricity, a bronze dragon can breathe a cone of repulsion gas. Targets must make a Will save or be compelled to do nothing but move away from the dragon for 1d6 rounds plus 1 round per age category. This is a mind-affecting compulsion effect."},{"type":"Spell-Like Abilities","kind":"Sp","details":"A bronze dragon gains the following spell-like abilities, usable at will upon reaching the listed age category. Very young-speak with animals; Juvenile-create food and water; Adult-fog cloud; Old-detect thoughts; Ancient-control water; Great wyrm-control weather."},{"type":"Tidal Wave","kind":"Su","details":"A great wyrm bronze dragon can cause the sea to rise up and crush his enemies once per day as a standard action. This affects an area of coastline 120 ft. in length and targets all creatures within 40 ft. of the shore-treat the targets as if struck by an avalanche. Treat all creatures as if they were in the bury zone. The save DC to halve this damage is equal to the dragon's breath weapon DC. Those who fail their saves take full damage and are drawn 60 ft. off shore and deposited 20 ft. under the surface on the round after the wave hits."},{"type":"Vortex","kind":"Ex","details":"Once per day, an ancient or older bronze dragon can create a vortex as a standard action, just like an elder water elemental. A bronze dragon can maintain this vortex for 1 round per age category."},{"type":"Water Breathing","kind":"Ex","details":"A bronze dragon breathes water and can use its breath weapon, spells, and abilities underwater."},{"type":"Wave Mastery","kind":"Su","details":"For up to 10 minutes per age category per day, a juvenile bronze dragon, along with creatures or vessels within 50 ft., can move at twice its normal speed in water. Age Category S pecial Abilities C aster Level Wyrmling Immunity to electricity, - repulsion breath, water breathing Very young Speak with animals - Young Change shape 1st Juvenile Wave mastery, create food and water 3rd Young adult DR 5/magic, spell resistance 5th Adult frightful presence, fog cloud 7th Mature adult DR 10/magic 9th Old Electricity aura, detect thoughts 11th Very old DR 15/magic 13th Ancient Vortex, control water 15th Wyrm DR 20/magic 17th Great wyrm Tidal wave, control weather 19th."}],"description":"Bronze dragons have been known to ally with travelers and adventurers if the cause and reward is right and just.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Adult Cloud Dragon","cr":13,"xp":25600,"alignment":"CN","size":"Huge","type":"dragon","subtypes":["air","extraplanar"],"init":3,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"},{"type":"mist vision"}],"auras":["frightful presence (180 ft., DC 22)"],"ac":29,"ac_touch":7,"ac_flat_footed":29,"ac_mods":"-1 Dex, +22 natural, -2 size","hp":184,"hd":"16d12+80","hdvalue":16,"fort":15,"ref":9,"will":13,"dr":"5/magic","immunities":["electricity","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":24,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"},{"type":"swim","speed":40}],"melee":"bite +22 (2d8+10/19-20), 2 claws +22 (2d6+7), tail slap +19 (2d6+10), 2 wings +19 (1d8+3)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"50-ft. cone, 12d8 electricity, DC 23"},{"type":"crush"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":16,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":21,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"fog cloud"},{"spell":"obscuring mist"},{"spell":"solid fog"}]}],"spellsknown_caster_level":5,"spellsknown_concentration":10,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"blur"},{"spell":"see invisibility"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"charm person"},{"spell":"detect secret doors"},{"spell":"shield"},{"spell":"true strike"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"dancing lights"},{"spell":"detect poison"},{"spell":"light"},{"spell":"message"},{"spell":"prestidigitation"},{"spell":"read magic"}]}],"strength":24,"dexterity":9,"constitution":21,"intelligence":16,"wisdom":20,"charisma":19,"baseatk":16,"cmb":24,"cmd":35,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Critical Focus"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Diplomacy)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite, claws)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Appraise","value":22},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":29},{"skill":"Fly","value":10},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":23},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":22},{"skill":"Perception","value":24},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":24},{"skill":"Stealth","value":10},{"skill":"Survival","value":24},{"skill":"Swim","value":15}],"languages":["Auran","Common","Draconic","Elven"],"sq":[{"type":"cloud form","details":"16 rounds/day"}],"environments":["any air (Plane of Air)"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"The blue-white scales of this four-horned dragon exude wisps of fog. The dragon's snout is short but filled with sharp teeth.","group":"Primal Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 2","special_abilities":[{"type":"Cloud Form","kind":"Su","details":"An adult or older cloud dragon can change itself into a cloudy vapor as a swift action for a number of rounds per day equal to its Hit Dice. This ability functions as gaseous form but the dragon's fly speed is unchanged."},{"type":"Cloud Breath","kind":"Su","details":"A great wyrm cloud dragon's breath weapon creates a cloud that persists in its cone shape for 1d4 rounds. Treat this cloud as a fog cloud that deals electricity damage equal to half the dragon's breath weapon damage to any creature that ends its turn still within the cloud (Reflex save halves the damage-DC equals the dragon's breath weapon save DC)."},{"type":"Mist Vision","kind":"Su","details":"A cloud dragon can see through fog, clouds, and similar obscuring effects with perfect clarity."},{"type":"Spell-Like Abilities","kind":"Sp","details":"A cloud dragon gains the following spell-like abilities, usable at will (unless indicated otherwise) on reaching the listed age category. Very young-obscuring mist; Young-fog cloud; Adult-solid fog; Old-cloudkill (3/day); Ancient-wind walk; Great wyrm-storm of vengeance (1/day)."},{"type":"Thundering Bite","kind":"Su","details":"An ancient or older cloud dragon's bite makes a thundering crash whenever it attacks, dealing an additional 2d6 points of sonic damage. A great wyrm's thundering bite deals an additional 4d6 sonic damage."}],"description":"Cloud dragons stay out of the complicated political schemes and obsessions of other dragons (especially the chromatic dragons), preferring to live their lives freely and as the whim to travel strikes them. Exploration and viewing new lands from far above are the cloud dragon's greatest joy, rivaled only by speaking with new creatures and gaining exotic treasures from them. They keep lairs on high mountain peaks, but are often away on journeys of discovery, returning home only when they've claimed a new treasure that needs to be placed in safekeeping back home.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Adult Lunar Dragon","cr":13,"xp":25600,"alignment":"CN","size":"Huge","type":"dragon","init":3,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"},{"type":"see in darkness"}],"auras":["alien presence (180 ft., DC 23)"],"ac":28,"ac_touch":7,"ac_flat_footed":28,"ac_mods":"-1 Dex, +21 natural, -2 size","hp":200,"hd":"16d12+96","hdvalue":16,"fort":15,"ref":9,"will":16,"defensive_abilities":["reflected light"],"dr":"5/magic","immunities":["cold","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":24,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"burrow","speed":20},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"bite +22 (2d8+12), 2 claws +22 (2d6+8), 2 wings +20 (2d6+4), tail slap +20 (2d8+12)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"bewildering breath"},{"type":"breath weapon","details":"100-ft. line, 12d8 cold, DC 23"},{"type":"crush"},{"type":"moonsilver"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":16,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":21,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"dancing lights"},{"spell":"life bubble"},{"spell":"moonstruck"}]}],"spellsknown_caster":"sorcerer","spellsknown_caster_level":7,"spellsknown_concentration":12,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":3,"spells":[{"spell":"haste"},{"spell":"heroism"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"blur"},{"spell":"hypnotic pattern"},{"spell":"mirror image"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"comprehend languages"},{"spell":"mage armor"},{"spell":"protection from evil"},{"spell":"shocking grasp"},{"spell":"vanish"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"arcane mark"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"light"},{"spell":"mage hand"},{"spell":"prestidigitation"},{"spell":"read magic"},{"spell":"resistance"}]}],"strength":27,"dexterity":9,"constitution":20,"intelligence":20,"wisdom":22,"charisma":21,"baseatk":16,"cmb":26,"cmd":35,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Arcane Strike"},{"feat":"Dazing Assault"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Toughness"},{"feat":"Wingover"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":12},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":24},{"skill":"Fly","value":10},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":24},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana, geography, history, local, nature)","value":20},{"skill":"Perception","value":25},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":25},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":24},{"skill":"Use Magic Device","value":24}],"languages":["Aklo","Aquan","Auran","Common","Draconic","Ignan"],"sq":[{"type":"no breath"},{"type":"starflight"}],"environments":["any vacuum"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"A shimmering halo surrounds this regal dragon's spine-crowned head, and its vast wings ripple like milky gossamer lit by the moon.","group":"Outer Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 4","special_abilities":[{"type":"Absolute Cold","kind":"Su","details":"An old or older lunar dragon's breath weapon can affect creatures immune to cold damage. A creature immune to cold damage still takes half damage from the breath weapon (no damage with a successful saving throw). Resistant creatures' cold resistance is treated as 10 less than normal."},{"type":"Alien Presence","kind":"Su","details":"A lunar dragon's alien presence affects opponents that fail their saves as touch of idiocy (or as feeblemind for creatures with 4 or fewer Hit Dice) for 5d6 rounds. This is a mind-affecting compulsion effect."},{"type":"Bewildering Breath","kind":"Su","details":"A creature that fails its saving throw against a lunar dragon's breath weapon emits light (as faerie fire) and is dazzled for 1d4 rounds. If the lunar dragon is adult or older, the creature is also confused for 1d4 rounds."},{"type":"Moonsilver","kind":"Ex","details":"A lunar dragon's natural weapons are treated as silver for the purpose of overcoming damage reduction."},{"type":"Reflect Rays","kind":"Su","details":"Rays and ranged touch effects that strike an ancient or older lunar dragon but fail to overcome its spell resistance are reflected back at their source, using the original attack roll to determine whether they hit."},{"type":"Reflected Light","kind":"Ex","details":"A very young or older lunar dragon can't be blinded or dazzled by bright light or patterns."}],"description":"Lunar dragons frequently interact with mortals, spending long hours watching the activities occurring on planets that interest them.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Adult Sky Dragon","cr":13,"xp":25600,"alignment":"LG","size":"Huge","type":"dragon","subtypes":["air"],"init":4,"senses":[{"type":"cloud sight"},{"type":"dragon senses"}],"auras":["frightful presence (180 ft., DC 23)"],"ac":29,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":29,"ac_mods":"+21 natural, -2 size","hp":184,"hd":"16d12+80","hdvalue":16,"fort":15,"ref":12,"will":17,"dr":"5/magic","immunities":["electricity","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":24,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"bite +22 (2d8+12/19-20), 2 claws +22 (2d6+8), gore +22 (2d6+12), tail slap +20 (2d6+12)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite and gore)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"50-ft. cone, 12d8 electricity damage, DC 23"},{"type":"crush","details":"DC 23, 2d8+12"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":16,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":21,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"detect evil"},{"spell":"feather fall"},{"spell":"gust of wind"}]}],"spellsknown_caster_level":7,"spellsknown_concentration":12,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"blink"},{"spell":"lightning bolt"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"glitterdust"},{"spell":"invisibility"},{"spell":"resist energy"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":8,"spells":[{"spell":"endure elements"},{"spell":"expeditious retreat"},{"spell":"magic missile"},{"spell":"obscuring mist"},{"spell":"shocking grasp"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"disrupt undead"},{"spell":"mage hand"},{"spell":"mending"},{"spell":"message"},{"spell":"ray of frost"},{"spell":"read magic"}]}],"strength":27,"dexterity":10,"constitution":21,"intelligence":20,"wisdom":21,"charisma":20,"baseatk":16,"cmb":26,"cmd":36,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Hover"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":16,"special":"+20 when jumping"},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":24},{"skill":"Fly","value":19},{"skill":"Heal","value":24},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana, geography, religion)","value":24},{"skill":"Perception","value":30},{"skill":"Perform (sing)","value":21},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":24},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":24}],"languages":["Auran","Celestial","Common","Draconic","Infernal","Sylvan"],"sq":[{"type":"borne aloft"},{"type":"change shape"}],"environments":["temperate mountains","warm mountains"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"Although wingless, this dragon twists gracefully though the sky, its scales ref lecting the shifting hues of the heavens.","group":"Imperial Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 3","special_abilities":[{"type":"Borne Aloft","kind":"Su","details":"Old or younger sky dragons fly with good maneuverability while all older sky dragons have perfect."},{"type":"Celestial Emissary","kind":"Su","details":"Three times per day, a great wyrm sky dragon can imbue others with the celestial aspect of the oracle spell divine vessel, but it can only be cast on another willing creature of good alignment."},{"type":"Change Shape","kind":"Su","details":"A young or older sky dragon can assume any humanoid form three times per day as if using polymorph."},{"type":"Cloud Sight","kind":"Su","details":"A very young or older sky dragon's sight isn't impeded by clouds or fog, or by spells that create areas of fog."},{"type":"Grounding Breath","kind":"Su","details":"Any flying creature damaged by the breath weapon of an ancient or older sky dragon must make a Fortitude save with the same DC as the sky dragon's breath weapon or lose the ability to fly for 1d4 rounds."},{"type":"Primal Lightning","kind":"Su","details":"An old or older sky dragon's breath weapon can affect creatures normally immune or resistant to electricity damage. A creature immune to electricity damage still takes half damage from the breath weapon (no damage with a successful saving throw). Resistant creatures' electricity resistance is treated as 10 less than normal."}],"description":"Benevolent and noble, sky dragons, or tienlungs, are fearsome champions of good and protectors of those in need. They are often sought out for their wise council, which they grant only to the deserving and true.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Adult Solar Dragon","cr":13,"xp":25600,"alignment":"LN","size":"Huge","type":"dragon","subtypes":["fire"],"init":5,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"},{"type":"see in darkness"}],"auras":["alien presence (180 ft., DC 23)"],"ac":28,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":27,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +19 natural, -2 size","hp":212,"hd":"17d12+102","hdvalue":17,"fort":15,"ref":13,"will":15,"dr":"5/magic","immunities":["fire","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":24,"weaknesses":["vulnerable to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"bite +24 (2d8+13), 2 claws +24 (2d6+9), tail slap +22 (2d6+13), 2 wings +22 (1d8+4)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"100-ft. line, 12d10 fire, DC 23"},{"type":"channel life","details":"8/day"},{"type":"crush"},{"type":"primal fire"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":7,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":12,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"cup of dust"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"searing light"}]}],"spellsknown_caster":"sorcerer","spellsknown_caster_level":7,"spellsknown_concentration":12,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"dispel magic"},{"spell":"tongues"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"invisibility"},{"spell":"resist energy"},{"spell":"scorching ray"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":8,"spells":[{"spell":"charm person"},{"spell":"color spray"},{"spell":"mage armor"},{"spell":"magic missile"},{"spell":"shield"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"bleed"},{"spell":"detect poison"},{"spell":"flare"},{"spell":"light"},{"spell":"mage hand"},{"spell":"prestidigitation"},{"spell":"read magic"}]}],"strength":28,"dexterity":13,"constitution":20,"intelligence":19,"wisdom":16,"charisma":21,"baseatk":17,"cmb":28,"cmd":39,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Quick Channel"},{"feat":"Selective Channeling"},{"feat":"Silent Spell"},{"feat":"Toughness"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":25},{"skill":"Fly","value":13},{"skill":"Heal","value":21},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":24},{"skill":"Knowledge (history)","value":24},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":24},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":24},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":24},{"skill":"Linguistics","value":9},{"skill":"Perception","value":23},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":23}],"languages":["Auran","Celestial","Common","Draconic","Ignan","Sylvan","Terran"],"sq":[{"type":"no breath"},{"type":"starflight"}],"environments":["any vacuum"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"This regal dragon glows like the sun. Its burnished wings shimmer the color of flames, and a crown of horns decorates its head.","group":"Outer Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 4","special_abilities":[{"type":"Alien Presence","kind":"Su","details":"A creature that fails its saving throw against a solar dragon's alien presence is blinded for 5d6 rounds (or permanently if it has 4 Hit Dice or fewer)."},{"type":"Beam of Light","kind":"Su","details":"A great wyrm solar dragon can transform itself into a beam of pure light and travel to any location it can see as a move action. This travel must be in a straight line, but otherwise the dragon can travel anywhere that light can enter."},{"type":"Channel Life","kind":"Su","details":"A solar dragon can channel positive energy a number of times per day equal to 3 + its Charisma modifier, using its age category + 2 as its cleric level. This energy can be used only to heal living creatures."},{"type":"Channel Radiation","kind":"Su","details":"An old or older solar dragon can use its channel life ability to instead channel radiation that deals an equal amount of damage to living creatures. A living creature that succeeds at a Fortitude save takes half damage."},{"type":"Primal Fire","kind":"Su","details":"A very young or older solar dragon's breath weapon can affect creatures normally immune or resistant to fire damage. A creature immune to fire damage still takes half damage from the breath weapon (no damage with a successful saving throw). A resistant creature's fire resistance is treated as 10 less than normal."}],"description":"Arrogant and proud, solar dragons see themselves as the originators of light and life in the vastness of space. They treat all living creatures as their own creations.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Adult Void Dragon","cr":13,"xp":25600,"alignment":"NE","size":"Huge","type":"dragon","init":5,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"},{"type":"see in darkness"}],"auras":["alien presence (180 ft., DC 23)"],"ac":29,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":28,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +20 natural, -2 size","hp":184,"hd":"16d12+80","hdvalue":16,"fort":15,"ref":11,"will":15,"dr":"5/magic","immunities":["cold","confusion","insanity effects","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":24,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"bite +23 (2d8+12/19-20 plus obliterate), 2 claws +22 (2d6+8), 2 wings +20 (1d8+4), tail slap +20 (2d6+12)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft. (15 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"50-ft. cone, 12d8 cold, DC 23"},{"type":"crush"},{"type":"obliterate","details":"DC 23"},{"type":"suffocating breath","details":"DC 23"},{"type":"void gaze","details":"DC 23"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":16,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":21,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"blur"},{"spell":"ray of enfeeblement"},{"spell":"ray of exhaustion"}]}],"spellsknown_caster":"sorcerer","spellsknown_caster_level":7,"spellsknown_concentration":12,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"dispel magic"},{"spell":"lightning bolt"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":7,"spells":[{"spell":"invisibility"},{"spell":"resist energy"},{"spell":"touch of idiocy"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":8,"spells":[{"spell":"alarm"},{"spell":"cause fear"},{"spell":"hypnotism"},{"spell":"mage armor"},{"spell":"obscuring mist"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"mage hand"},{"spell":"read magic"},{"spell":"4 more"}]}],"strength":27,"dexterity":12,"constitution":21,"intelligence":20,"wisdom":17,"charisma":20,"baseatk":16,"cmb":26,"cmd":37,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Hover"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"},{"feat":"Wingover"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":17},{"skill":"Bluff","value":24},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":18},{"skill":"Fly","value":20},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":22},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":24},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":24},{"skill":"Perception","value":22},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":22},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":20},{"skill":"Stealth","value":12},{"skill":"Survival","value":14},{"skill":"Use Magic Device","value":16}],"languages":["Abyssal","Aklo","Celestial","Draconic","Ignan","Infernal"],"sq":[{"type":"agile"},{"type":"no breath"},{"type":"starflight"}],"environments":["any vacuum"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"This dragon's ebony scales and horns are flecked with a substance that glows an eerie green. The folds of its wings reflect a starry sky.","group":"Outer Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 4","special_abilities":[{"type":"Agile","kind":"Ex","details":"Void dragons have good aerial maneuverability regardless of their age or size."},{"type":"Alien Presence","kind":"Su","details":"A void dragon's alien presence causes an opponent that fails its save to be overcome with dizziness, becoming sickened (or nauseated if the target has 4 or fewer Hit Dice) for 5d6 rounds."},{"type":"Obliterate","kind":"Su","details":"A young or older void dragon's bite deals an additional 2d6 points of negative energy damage. A creature reduced to 0 or fewer hit points by this attack must succeed at a Fortitude save or be immediately slain and reduced to ashes (as the disintegrate spell). The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Suffocating Breath","kind":"Su","details":"Instead of dealing cold damage, a very young or older void dragon can breathe a cone-shaped suffocation effect. An air-dependent creature that fails its Fortitude save suffocates for a number of rounds equal to the dragon's age category. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Void Gaze","kind":"Su","details":"A creature within 30 ft. of an adult or older void dragon must succeed at a Will save or become confused for 1d6 rounds. This gaze attack is a mind-affecting effect. The save DC is Charisma-based."}],"description":"Void dragons have been tainted by long exposure to the terrible alien entities that dwell in deep space. Though some continue to struggle against the inevitable tide of annihilation, many have embraced the encroaching void and exist only to feed and destroy.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Akhlut","cr":13,"xp":25600,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"magical beast","subtypes":["cold","shapechanger"],"init":6,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"},{"type":"snow vision"}],"ac":30,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":27,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +1 dodge, +19 natural, -2 size","hp":189,"hd":"18d10+90","hdvalue":18,"fort":16,"ref":13,"will":10,"dr":"15/magic","immunities":["cold"],"weaknesses":["vulnerability to fire"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"swim","speed":60}],"melee":"bite +27 (4d8+15/15-20 plus 4d6 cold and grab)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"savage bite"},{"type":"shore storming"},{"type":"swallow whole","details":"2d8+15 bludgeoning damage plus 4d6 cold, AC 19, 18 hp"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":18,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":23,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"control weather","details":"windy or cold weather only"}]}],"strength":31,"dexterity":15,"constitution":20,"intelligence":4,"wisdom":15,"charisma":6,"baseatk":18,"cmb":30,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":43,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Stealth)"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":2,"special":"+6 when jumping"},{"skill":"Perception","value":14},{"skill":"Stealth","value":16,"special":"+28 in snow"},{"skill":"Swim","value":18}],"languages":["Aquan (cannot speak)"],"sq":[{"type":"change shape","details":"orca; beast shape III"},{"type":"hold breath"},{"type":"snow walking"}],"environments":["cold lakes","any oceans","any plains"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"A dorsal fin rises up from the back of this immense black-and-white-furred, wolf-like beast.","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 3","special_abilities":[{"type":"Savage Bite","kind":"Ex","details":"An akhlut's bite threatens a critical hit on a roll of 18-20."},{"type":"Shore Storming","kind":"Ex","details":"An akhlut automatically transforms into an orca whenever it is fully immersed in water, losing its legs and fur. Likewise, when an akhlut emerges from the water, it automatically transforms into its wolf-orca hybrid form. If an akhlut moves from water to land (or vice versa) on the round before initiating combat, it gains a +8 bonus on its initiative check. This initial attack resolves as a charge. An akhlut has the same statistics in both forms."},{"type":"Snow Vision","kind":"Ex","details":"An akhlut can see perfectly well in snowy conditions, and doesn't take any penalties on Perception checks while in snowy weather."},{"type":"Snow Walking","kind":"Su","details":"An akhlut can walk on snow or thin sheets of ice as though affected by water walk. It only leaves a trail on such surfaces when it wants to."}],"description":"Resembling nothing so much as a killer whale mixed with a wolf, the rarely seen akhlut stalks frigid seas and the frozen lands nearby, shrouded by perpetual blizzards. Legend holds that the first akhlut was born fully-formed in the eye of a polar hurricane, the merciless anger of the elements made flesh. Whether or not the tale is true, the akhlut's ferocity is certainly as memorable as that of any storm.\n\nWhile the akhlut appears as a wolf-orca hybrid on land, when it enters the water, its legs and fur vanish and it transforms fully into the form of an orca. Akhluts are particularly skilled at charging into and out of water, their transformation between shapes occurring in the blink of an eye.\n\nEach akhlut fiercely defends its hunting grounds from other predators, and especially against other akhluts.\n\nWhile this does reduce the number of dangerous predators in a region, it's unclear whether replacing lesser predators with something as dangerous as an akhlut is actually preferable. Typically, an akhlut considers its territory to be the boundaries of the storm created by its control weather spell-like ability, and rarely travels far from this storm's borders.\n\nAn akhlut is 22 ft. long and weighs 8,000 pounds.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Alraune","cr":13,"xp":25600,"alignment":"NE","size":"Large","type":"plant","init":5,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"}],"auras":["calming fragrance (60 ft., DC 24)"],"ac":27,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":26,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +17 natural, -1 size","hp":199,"hd":"19d8+114","hdvalue":19,"fort":17,"ref":9,"will":11,"immunities":["plant traits"],"sr":24,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40}],"melee":"4 vines +20 (1d10+7 plus grab and bleed)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"bleed","details":"2d6"},{"type":"constrict","details":"1d10+10"},{"type":"feed"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":13,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":19,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"charm monster"},{"spell":"detect thoughts"},{"spell":"suggestion"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"commune with nature"},{"spell":"mind fog"},{"spell":"wall of thorns"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"hold monster"},{"spell":"quickened glitterdust"}]}],"strength":24,"dexterity":13,"constitution":22,"intelligence":10,"wisdom":17,"charisma":21,"baseatk":14,"cmb":22,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":33,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Deceitful"},{"feat":"Great Cleave"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Quicken Spell-Like Ability (glitterdust)"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":16},{"skill":"Disguise","value":9},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":9},{"skill":"Perception","value":17},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":14}],"languages":["Aklo","Common","Elven","Sylvan"],"environments":["temperate forests"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"An attractive green-skinned woman sits in the depths of this enormous, sweet-smelling flower.","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 3","special_abilities":[{"type":"Calming Fragrance","kind":"Su","details":"A supernaturally sweet perfume that calms the nerves and blunts aggression constantly surrounds an alraune to a radius of 60 ft. Any creature in this area of effect must make a DC 24 Will save at the start of its turn to avoid falling under the effects of calm emotions for 1 round. Creatures that could be attracted to the alraune's current apparent gender take a -2 penalty on this Will save, while all other creatures gain a +2 bonus on the save. This is a mind-affecting effect. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Feed","kind":"Ex","details":"An alraune's roots can feed on a helpless or willing target. At the end of an hour of feeding, the victim takes 1d6 points of both Constitution and Intelligence drain, and the alraune heals 3d6 points of damage."}],"description":"An alraune relies on its supernaturally soothing odor to render enemies incapable of making hostile acts against it-even if the alraune attacks a foe, its calming scent can wipe away any thoughts of violence from its prey. At rest, an alraune appears to be merely a large thorny plant with a single enormous and brightly colored flower at its center.\n\nWhen an alraune attacks, its thorny vines lash out and its flower blooms, revealing an attractive, green-skinned humanoid form within. An alraune's apparent gender can vary even from encounter to encounter, for the plant can reshape its humanoid portions as it desires to increase the likelihood of setting its victims at ease. Regardless of the plant's apparent gender, it is itself asexual and reproduces (typically once or twice per decade) by budding a single offspring over the course of a spring season.\n\nDespite their appearance, alraunes are quite mobile (capable of walking almost like a spider upon their numerous long roots and thorny vines). They hunt by using commune with nature to locate potential prey, preferring humanoid flesh over all others. When an alraune needs prey, it uses its mind-affecting abilities to convince foes to dig their own graves and bury themselves-once a foe is helplessly buried in the soil, the alraune can feed from it via its flesh-burrowing roots, converting the victim's blood and memories into the strange nutrients it so craves.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Argus","cr":13,"xp":25600,"alignment":"LN","size":"Gargantuan","type":"aberration","subtypes":["mythic"],"init":12,"init_special":"mythic","senses":[{"type":"all-around vision"},{"type":"arcane sight"},{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"detect scrying"},{"type":"limitless vision"},{"type":"mistsight"},{"type":"see in darkness"},{"type":"true seeing"}],"auras":["frightful presence (40 ft., DC 16)"],"ac":30,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":28,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +4 insight, +18 natural, -4 size","hp":184,"hd":"13d8+126","hdvalue":13,"fort":10,"ref":6,"will":9,"defensive_abilities":["absolute readiness","rock catching"],"dr":"10/epic","immunities":["blindness","dazzled"],"resists":[{"type":"cold","value":30},{"type":"fire","value":30}],"weaknesses":["vulnerable to fascination and sleep"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40}],"melee":"2 claws +20 (3d6+14 plus grab), bite +19 (2d8+14)","ranged":"rock +8 (3d6+14)","space":"20 ft.","reach":"20 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"accurate strikes"},{"type":"constrict","details":"3d6+14"},{"type":"eye gouge"},{"type":"fascinating gaze"},{"type":"mythic power","details":"6/day, surge +1d8"},{"type":"rend","details":"2 claws, 3d6+21"},{"type":"rock throwing","details":"200 ft."}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":14,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":20,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"arcane sight"},{"spell":"detect scrying"},{"spell":"true seeing"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"arcane eye"},{"spell":"clairaudience/ clairvoyance"},{"spell":"status"},{"spell":"true strike"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"quickened true strike"}]}],"strength":39,"dexterity":14,"constitution":23,"intelligence":13,"wisdom":12,"charisma":10,"baseatk":9,"cmb":27,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":43,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness","type":"mythic"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes","type":"mythic"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative","type":"mythic"},{"feat":"Intimidating Prowess"},{"feat":"Quicken Spell-Like Ability (true strike)"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (claw)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":24},{"skill":"Handle Animal","value":6},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":30},{"skill":"Knowledge (history)","value":10},{"skill":"Perception","value":29,"special":"+37 on vision-based Perception checks"},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":23},{"skill":"Swim","value":24}],"languages":["Aklo","Celestial","Common"],"environments":["any land"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This misshapen giant is covered in horns, tumorous tentacles, unsightly warts, and strange, staring eyes.","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 4","special_abilities":[{"type":"Absolute Readiness","kind":"Ex","details":"An argus is never surprised or flat-footed. It can act in the surprise round as if it were a normal round."},{"type":"Accurate Strikes","kind":"Ex","details":"An argus's attacks ignore the AC bonus granted to targets by any cover less than total cover, and the miss chance granted to targets by any concealment less than total concealment."},{"type":"Eye Gouge","kind":"Ex","details":"If an argus rends or pins an opponent, as a swift action it can attempt a dirty trick maneuver to blind the target. If its combat maneuver check exceeds the DC by 10 or more, the opponent is permanently blinded."},{"type":"Fascinating Gaze","kind":"Su","details":"A creature within 40 ft. of an argus must succeed at a DC 16 Will saving throw or be fascinated for 5d6 rounds. If the creature has 4 or fewer Hit Dice, it is instead dazed for 5d6 rounds. An argus can't use this ability in the same round it uses frightful presence. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Limitless Vision","kind":"Ex","details":"An argus takes no distance penalties on Perception checks."}],"description":"An argus is an ancient creature related to the titans, transformed by a deity into a vigilant and restless sentry, usually as a punishment for some affront or rebellion. Within its hideous and misshapen body lies a lonely heart that craves music and beauty to comfort it in its forlorn and unending vigil. It might talk peaceably with visitors if they promise to sing songs or tell stories (and it believes its guests don't intend to harm it or steal what it guards). If insulted or mocked, an argus is quick to anger, dispatching foes so it can go back to brooding in peace. An argus stands 25 ft. tall and weighs 18,000 pounds.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Azruverda","cr":13,"xp":25600,"alignment":"CG","size":"Huge","type":"aberration","init":2,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"100 ft."}],"ac":25,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":23,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +15 natural, -2 size","hp":168,"hd":"16d8+96","hdvalue":16,"fort":11,"ref":7,"will":15,"dr":"10/magic and slashing","immunities":["acid"],"resists":[{"type":"cold","value":10}],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50},{"type":"climb","speed":30}],"melee":"bite +21 (2d6+11), 2 claws +21 (1d10+11)","ranged":"acid spit +13 touch (10d6 acid)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"acid spit"},{"type":"rend","details":"1d10+11"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":16,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":22,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"dancing lights"},{"spell":"faerie fire"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"daylight"},{"spell":"giant vermin"},{"spell":"insect plague"},{"spell":"repel vermin"},{"spell":"summon swarm"}]}],"strength":32,"dexterity":15,"constitution":23,"intelligence":14,"wisdom":16,"charisma":25,"baseatk":12,"cmb":25,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. bull rush","cmd":37,"cmd_special":"+2 vs. bull rush, +8 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Awesome Blow"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Greater Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Improved Bull Rush"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Point-Blank Shot"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (acid spit)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":26},{"skill":"Handle Animal","value":17},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":26},{"skill":"Knowledge (dungeoneering)","value":12},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":12},{"skill":"Perception","value":22},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":13},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":15},{"skill":"Survival","value":16}],"languages":["Aklo","Common","Undercommon"],"sq":[{"type":"vermin master"}],"environments":["any underground"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","brood (3-7)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"A humanoid head peers forth from this enormous creature's beautifully iridescent, spike-covered beetle carapace.","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 3","special_abilities":[{"type":"Acid Spit","kind":"Ex","details":"An azruverda can spit a stream of acid at a target within 60 ft. as a ranged touch attack that deals 10d6 points of acid damage."},{"type":"Vermin Master","kind":"Su","details":"An azruverda can mentally control to up to 32 HD (twice the azruverda's racial Hit Dice) of vermin at any one time through a combination of supernatural pheromones and magical manipulation. To control a vermin, the azruverda must be able to see it, and it must be within 120 ft. Attempting to control a vermin is a standard action-the vermin can resist this attempt with a DC 25 Will save. If the vermin fails this save, the azruverda can issue a simple mental command like \"fight,\" \"come here,\" \"go there,\" or \"stand still\" as a swift action. Though composed of thousands of individuals, vermin with the swarm subtype are vulnerable to this ability as well. An azruverda can release a creature from this control as a free action. Vermin affected by this ability act normally unless an azruverda is actively controlling it, but never attack their master azruverda. The save DC is Charisma-based."}],"description":"Although repulsive in shape, these enormous, human-faced insectoid creatures are generally peaceful and serene. Left to its own devices, an azruverda is typically content to cultivate fungal gardens in deep underground sanctuaries. These gardens are beautiful to behold—masterful combinations of fungi, rocks, and other objects arranged in an artistic manner. Although generally solitary, azruverdas collaborate when a threat intrudes upon one of their underground homes.\n\nAzruverdas stand 16 ft. tall on their many legs and weigh close to 4,000 pounds.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Banshee","cr":13,"xp":25600,"alignment":"CE","size":"Medium","type":"undead","subtypes":["incorporeal"],"init":15,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"hear heartbeat"}],"ac":26,"ac_touch":26,"ac_flat_footed":14,"ac_mods":"+4 deflection, +11 Dex, +1 dodge","hp":161,"hd":"19d8+76","hdvalue":19,"fort":10,"ref":19,"will":18,"defensive_abilities":["incorporeal"],"immunities":["undead traits"],"weaknesses":["sunlight powerlessness"],"speed":[{"type":"fly","speed":60,"maneuverability":"perfect"}],"melee":"incorporeal touch +26 (14d6 negative energy plus terror)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"wail"}],"dexterity":32,"intelligence":5,"wisdom":20,"charisma":19,"baseatk":14,"cmb":25,"cmd":40,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Mobility"},{"feat":"Step Up"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (touch)"},{"feat":"Wind Stance"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":19},{"skill":"Perception","value":31},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":7}],"languages":["Common","Elven"],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This beautiful, ghostly elven woman glides through the air, her long hair flowing around a face knotted into a mask of rage.","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 2","special_abilities":[{"type":"Hear Heartbeat","kind":"Ex","details":"A banshee can sense the beating hearts of living creatures within 60 ft., as if it had the blindsight ability."},{"type":"Terror","kind":"Su","details":"A creature damaged by the banshee's touch attack must make a DC 23 Will save. Failure means that the victim cowers in fear for 1d3 rounds. If a target is protected against fear by a dispellable effect (such as heroes' feast or mind blank), the banshee's touch attempts to dispel one such effect with greater dispel magic (CL 14th). Negative energy damage caused by a banshee's touch can only harm the living; it cannot heal undead. This is a mind-affecting fear effect. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Wail","kind":"Su","details":"Once per minute, a banshee may wail as a full-round action. The wail lasts until the beginning of her next turn. All creatures within 40 ft. of the banshee when she begins her wail, as well as all creatures that end their turn within that radius, must make a DC 23 Fortitude save. (This save is only required once per wail.) Creatures under the effects of a fear effect take a -4 penalty on this save. Creatures that make their save are sickened for 1d6 rounds. Those that fail take 140 points of damage (as if affected by a CL 14 wail of the banshee). If a wailing banshee is damaged during a wail, she must make a Will save (DC 15 + damage taken) to maintain the wail; otherwise it ends. This is a sonic death effect. Banshee wails are supernaturally powerful, and penetrate the effect of any spell of 3rd level or lower that creates silence. The save DC is Charisma-based."}],"description":"A banshee is the enraged spirit of an elven woman who either betrayed those she loved or was herself betrayed.\n\nMaddened by grief, a banshee visits her vengeance on all living creatures-innocent or guilty-with her fearsome touch and deadly wails.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""}];
